SCOPE — THIS LICENCE DOES NOT COVER THE BUNDLED FONTS

The MIT grant above applies to the source code of this project only.

It does NOT apply to the font files in `public/fonts/`. Those are
third-party typefaces, obtained under their own separate licences, and are
merely distributed alongside this software. They are not the copyright of the
holder named above, who therefore cannot and does not grant any rights in
them.

Every bundled font has additionally been modified: a set of ten honorific
symbol glyphs was merged into each file so those symbols render regardless of
which typeface is selected. Modifying a font can trigger obligations under
its licence — renaming requirements for reserved font names, notices that
must travel with the file, or restrictions on redistribution altogether.

One case is documented in full as the worked example: `HarfCanvasDiwani.ttf`
is a Modified Version of Layla Diwani (SIL Open Font License, Mohammed Isam),
renamed as the OFL requires because the upstream reserves its name. Its
licence text and a note on what was changed are in
`public/fonts/HarfCanvasDiwani-OFL.txt`, which must stay with that font file.

The provenance and licence terms of the remaining font files are not
documented in this repository. If you intend to redistribute this project, or
any font from it, you must establish each file's licence and its
modification terms for yourself first. Do not assume the MIT grant above
extends to them, because it does not.
